 # Local AI Workspace for Android
 
 An Android-first, offline-by-default AI workspace with a runtime-neutral Model Manager. The app keeps projects, chats, imported documents, local retrieval evidence, memory and model metadata in an on-device Room database. Model binaries stay in app-private storage; they are never stored in Room.
+
+Version **0.1.11** prepares the last selected usable LiteRT model from application startup, with real **Active model** loading/integrity/ready/error/cancel/retry in Workspace. Closing a chat does not cancel shared preparation; new chats use the remembered selection and isolated native conversation state. A ready/running identical preparation is shared, and the idle engine no longer has a ten-minute expiry. Worker-lifetime receipts avoid repeated SHA scans of unchanged private files. One engine remains resident: switching models/context/vision/backend, memory pressure or Android process reclamation can still require loading. GGUF retains its existing first-send path; CPU decode speed and the prior semantic relevance failure are unchanged.
+
+146app tests executed/PASS;2compatibility tests UP-TO-DATE; debug/release build and signature PASS; lint0errors/73pre-existing warnings. Room remains schema3; models/history/projects are preserved. New physical UI/native/timing validation **NOT_EXECUTED**. [Implementation and phone checks](docs/APP_MODEL_PREPARATION_011.md). [Artifact](docs/validation/apk-011.json).
+
+[Download0.1.11 APK from Drive](https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xOJPIKlK9cA4csUT-yphfqR9a9ijf1u_/view?usp=drivesdk) (91.58MB / 87.34MiB, ARM64,versionCode12). Install as an update without clearing data.
+
+## Previous release — 0.1.10
 
 Version **0.1.10** reorganizes Workspace around **Start chat** and optional **Start project**. Standalone chats and projects have separate lists and confirmed deletion; projects can contain multiple independently addressed chats and shared files/memory. Delete project removes its card and all owned chats/private documents/indexes/embeddings/project memory; deleting one project chat keeps its siblings and shared resources. Installed models and global memory remain. Existing projects are preserved by Room2→3 migration; deleted Personal workspace is no longer recreated at startup. Private-file cleanup has a durable retry outbox. [Behavior and phone checks](docs/WORKSPACE_010.md).
 
